<Page title="Privacy Policy | RDB Building Services LTD" description="How RDB Building Services LTD handles website enquiries, contact information and your data protection rights.">
<section class="wrap service-intro"><div class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><span>Privacy Policy</span></div><p class="eyebrow">YOUR INFORMATION</p><h1>Privacy Policy</h1></section>
<article class="wrap legal-content">
<h2>Who is responsible?</h2><p>R D B BUILDING SERVICES LTD, trading as RDB Building Services LTD, is responsible for the personal information handled for our business enquiries. Our company number is 16900008, registered in England and Wales.</p><p>For privacy questions, email <a href="mailto:info@rdbbuildingservices.co.uk">info@rdbbuildingservices.co.uk</a> or write to our business location: Unit 1, Newlands Farm, Newlands Lane, The Royal Town of Sutton Coldfield, Curdworth, Sutton Coldfield B76 0BE, United Kingdom.</p>
<h2>Information you provide</h2><p>Our enquiry forms request your name, email address, project details and service interest. You may also provide a telephone number, site postcode, budget and preferred timescale. Only fields marked as required must be completed. Please avoid sending sensitive personal information or unnecessary information about other people.</p>
<h2>How the forms work</h2><p>When you select “Send enquiry”, the form submits your entries to FormSubmit, a third-party form-processing service. It processes the request, may present a spam check and forwards the enquiry to info@rdbbuildingservices.co.uk. You do not need an email application to submit a form.</p><p>We do not store form entries in application cookies, local storage or a website database. FormSubmit and the systems used to deliver and receive email handle the information needed to process your enquiry. Read <a href="https://formsubmit.co/privacy.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">FormSubmit’s privacy information</a> for details of its practices.</p>
<h2>Why we use your information</h2><p>We use enquiry information to answer your questions, discuss suitability and requirements, prepare requested quotations and arrange any agreed next steps. Where you enquire about entering a contract with us personally, processing necessary to take those requested steps is based on taking steps before a contract. For general correspondence and enquiries on behalf of an organisation, we rely on our legitimate interests in responding to relevant business communications.</p><p>Information received through an enquiry is not permission for unrelated marketing. If a different purpose or additional information is needed, we will explain it as appropriate.</p>
<h2>Service providers and sharing</h2><p>Information may be handled by service providers supporting form processing, spam prevention, email delivery and storage, and technical security. Access should be limited to what is needed for those purposes. We may disclose information where required by law or where necessary to establish, exercise or defend legal rights.</p><p>We do not claim that all processing takes place in the UK. Service locations and international processing arrangements depend on the providers involved. Where restricted international transfers occur, applicable data protection requirements must be met.</p>
<h2>How long information is kept</h2><p>FormSubmit states that it retains form submissions for 30 days. RDB retains enquiry correspondence according to its purpose, including answering the request, managing any resulting project and meeting applicable legal or record-keeping requirements. Information should not be kept longer than necessary. You can contact us about the information held for a particular enquiry.</p>

<h2>Your rights</h2><p>Depending on the circumstances, UK data protection law provides rights to access, correct or erase personal information, restrict processing, object to certain uses and request portability. Rights and exceptions depend on the processing involved. If we rely on consent for a particular activity, you can withdraw it without affecting earlier lawful processing.</p>
<h2>External services and cookies</h2><p>Maps and reference links open separate websites with their own privacy practices. FormSubmit is contacted when you submit a form; its processing and any hosted spam-check step are described above. Read our <a href="/cookie-policy/">Cookie Policy</a> for more information about browser storage and external services.</p>
</article></Page>
